{#
  A page for a business you ring rather than browse.

  The old version of this direction was a 12-column grid with an electric
  accent and 12px-radius cards, which is the agency look — and `suits`
  included "trade", so plumbers were being shown an agency page. The grid
  encoded nothing true about the business; it was structure as decoration.

  What is true about a plumber's page is that someone arrives at it in a
  hurry, on a phone, holding something with one hand, and needs exactly two
  facts: do you come to my suburb, and what is the number. So the number is
  the largest type here and it never leaves the screen — bottom-fixed on a
  phone where the thumb already is, top-sticky on a desktop.

  Everything else is deliberately plain. The boldness is spent once.

  The type pairing is the other idea: a condensed display against Verdana,
  which is the widest and most legible sans present on every platform a small
  business owner's customer might be holding. Condensed against wide is a
  real contrast; -apple-system against -apple-system, which is what this
  direction had before, is not a pairing at all.

  This is still default_direction, so it has to hold up for a business nobody
  categorised. A sticky phone number degrades sanely for almost anything;
  without a phone the bar carries the address instead.
#}
{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block style %}
body{font-family:Verdana,'Lucida Grande','DejaVu Sans',sans-serif;font-size:17px}
{# Room for the fixed bar so it never covers the footer. #}
@media(max-width:819px){body{padding-bottom:5.5rem}}

.callout{background:{{ palette.accent }};color:{{ palette.paper }};
  display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.25rem 1rem;
  padding:.85rem 1.5rem;z-index:10}
.callout .label{font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;
  opacity:.85;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace}
.callout .number{font-family:'Avenir Next Condensed','Futura Condensed',
  'Arial Narrow',Helvetica,sans-serif;
  font-size:clamp(1.9rem,7vw,2.6rem);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.01em;
  line-height:1;text-decoration:none}
@media(max-width:819px){
  .callout{position:fixed;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;justify-content:center;
    box-shadow:0 -1px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.18)}
}
@media(min-width:820px){
  .callout{position:sticky;top:0;justify-content:flex-end;
    padding-right:max(1.5rem,calc((100vw - 66rem)/2))}
}

.hero{padding:4rem 1.5rem 2.5rem;display:grid;gap:2rem}
@media(min-width:820px){.hero{grid-template-columns:7fr 5fr;align-items:end}}
h1{font-family:'Avenir Next Condensed','Futura Condensed','Arial Narrow',
  Helvetica,sans-serif;
  font-size:clamp(2.6rem,9vw,5.5rem);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0;
  line-height:.98;margin:0;text-transform:uppercase}
.lede{margin-top:1.2rem;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.6;max-width:34rem;opacity:.8}

h2{font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.7rem;text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.16em;opacity:.5;margin:0 0 1.4rem}
h3{font-family:'Avenir Next Condensed','Futura Condensed','Arial Narrow',
  Helvetica,sans-serif;
  font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;margin:2rem 0 .6rem}
.band{padding:3.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(127,127,127,.22)}

{# Data set as data. Hours and service areas are the two things worth
   checking before ringing, so they get the utility face rather than prose. #}
.facts-grid{display:grid;gap:2.5rem}
@media(min-width:700px){.facts-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
.facts p{font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75}

{# No cards, no radius, no borders anywhere — see the note above. #}
.item{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(127,127,127,.16)}
{# The base sheet colours prices with the accent. Here the accent means "this
   is the thing you press", so a price wearing it dilutes the one signal the
   page has. Prices go back to ink. #}
.item .price{color:inherit;opacity:.75}
.hero-img{max-height:26rem;object-fit:cover}
.gallery{gap:.5rem}
{% endblock %}

{% block menu %}
{# "Menu" is the base's word for this section, which is right for a cafe and
   wrong for a plumber — and wrong again for whatever unmatched trade lands
   here via default_direction. "Services" covers all three. #}
  {% if menu %}
  <section class="band">
    <h2>Services</h2>
    {% for group, items in menu_groups %}
      {% if group %}<h3>{{ group }}</h3>{% endif %}
      {% for item in items %}
      <div class="item">
        <span class="name">{{ item.name }}
          {% if item.description %}<span class="desc">{{ item.description }}</span>{% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="dots"></span>
        <span class="price">{{ item.price or "—" }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% else %}
  <section class="band">
    <h2>Services</h2>
    <span class="sample">{{ sample_note }}</span>
    <p>{{ menu_sample }}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block hero %}
{% if phone %}
<div class="callout">
  <span class="label">Call</span>
  <a class="number" href="tel:{{ phone_href }}">{{ phone }}</a>
</div>
{% elif address %}
<div class="callout">
  <span class="label">Find us</span>
  <span class="number">{{ address }}</span>
</div>
{% endif %}
<header class="hero">
  <div class="hero-text">
    <h1>{{ business }}</h1>
    {% if about %}<p class="lede">{{ about }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if images %}<img class="hero-img" src="{{ images[0] }}" alt="">{% endif %}
  {% if stock_used %}<p class="credit">{{ stock_note }}</p>{% endif %}
</header>
{% endblock %}
